{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e2e1443f-34fc-4083-9a43-d49ed94a71c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# VisualAstro Color Guide\n",
    "\n",
    "VisualAstro offers many new colorsets and colormaps to choose from, as well as color manipulation tools!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "df3ffc28-de10-4436-a2a8-c0f88398302f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import visualastro as va\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.style.use('stix')\n",
    "va.config.figsize = (5,5)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ab6fb3f2-2b30-4fba-a6e3-a2b3caba8280",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Getting Colors in VisualAstro\n",
    "VisualAstro recognizes many colors, from Matplotlib's `named colors` to custom defined colorsets! To access any one of these colors use `get_colors`. This function is aware of many different named colors, color formats (hex, rgb, rgba), and custom colorsets. \n",
    "\n",
    "We can view our colors at any time by displaying color swatches with `va.help.color`, or by using the example plot given by `va.plot_colorset`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "30e923a2-bdee-40e3-b66d-0ceea05d76c9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "turbo6 colorset:  ['#35359a', '#4f65ff', '#5bffd9', '#c4ff05', '#ff7d3c', '#ab0449']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# get the turbo6 colorset\n",
    "turbo6 = va.get_colors('turbo6')\n",
    "print('turbo6 colorset: ', turbo6)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "c7aaf707-c76c-4403-a3ec-86ac479344b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x100 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# named colors:\n",
    "# any matplotlib named color, visualastro named color, xkcd color with or without 'xkcd:' !!!\n",
    "va.help.color(va.get_colors(['darkslateblue', 'ibmpnk', 'unicorn', 'duck egg blue', 'xkcd:dark periwinkle']))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "a094ea47-0031-4d42-ac86-4d4ad5588faf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 500x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x100 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# view example plot, and color swatches:\n",
    "va.plot_colorset('turbo6')\n",
    "va.help.color('turbo6', show_color_name=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "86374b5d-27ff-4f42-9dce-0cc4123f7be4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Modifying Saturation and Hue of an Existing Colorset\n",
    "\n",
    "We can change a colorset easily in VisualAstro using the `transform` keyword argument. Available transform options are `'saturate'`, `'desaturate'`, and `'lighten'`, with the intensity of each effect controlled by `factor`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "97bbeea7-0e3c-438d-9778-f220b5af5776",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x100 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x100 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x100 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "va.help.color(\n",
    "    va.get_colors(\n",
    "        ['#35359a', '#4f65ff', '#5bffd9', '#c4ff05', '#ff7d3c', '#ab0449'], \n",
    "        transform='lighten', \n",
    "        factor=0.2\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "va.help.color(va.get_colors('astro_seq', transform='saturate', factor=1))\n",
    "va.help.color(va.get_colors('astro_seq', transform='desaturate', factor=0.5))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "df4c4fc0-82da-436f-80a8-748975e65fff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Only one transform can be applied at the same time. To stack transforms, call the transformation functions `saturate_colors`, `desaturate_colors`, and `lighten_colors` directly on the returned colorset.
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a2ea7381-a27f-44e3-903d-744032c6e79c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Sampling Colors From a Colormap\n",
    "\n",
    "You can also pass an integer to `get_colors` to sample `N` colors from a colormap `cmap`. Set the range of the colormap with `cmap_range`, which by default is `(0,1)` (meaning the entire range of the colormap will be used). This can be done directly with the `sample_cmap` function."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "37bf57e6-b7fc-4dce-b8ab-852387af3eb3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x100 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x100 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x600 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "va.help.color(va.get_colors(6, cmap='cosmic', cmap_range=[0.3,1]))\n",
    "turbo = va.get_colors(10, cmap='turbo', cmap_range=[0.04,1])\n",
    "va.help.color(turbo)\n",
    "\n",
    "emerald = va.get_colors(6, cmap='emerald', cmap_range=[0.3,1], transform='saturate', factor=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12,6))\n",
    "va.plot_colorset(turbo, ax=ax[0])\n",
    "va.plot_colorset(emerald, ax=ax[1])\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9ffcd332-35e4-426b-8a92-8d3a37bef49a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Color Vision Deficiency (CVD) Simulations\n",
    "\n",
    "We can also view how our colorset looks like under different CVD spaces such as `'deuteranomaly'`, `'protanomaly'`, `'tritanomaly'`.\n",
    "Pass any one of these to the `cvd_type` argument and `get_colors` returns what the colorset would look like in a colorblind colorspace. You can also pass in `'d'`, `'p'`, or `'t'` as a shorthand."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "c6a74e5e-cf1e-4d66-8ba4-baebf0d4c298",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x100 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "va.help.color(va.get_colors('turbo6', cvd_type='deuteranomaly', severity=100))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "16b8b604-0d4c-42f5-8ab5-5db6f4da43c3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "You can also simulate the CVD space directly with `help.color`. We can pass in `'all'` to `cvd_type` to show all 3 types! As you can see, `'turbo6'` is colorblind safe!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "723f5192-fcfa-4b5c-8641-20c6400fe242",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x400 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "va.help.color('turbo6', cvd_type='all', show_color_name=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7a631e7d-ea98-4dd4-8475-78874a05b0f6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Advanced CVD Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "We can also plot the $\\Delta E*$ of a colorset, which computes the pairwise color difference matrix of a colorset in `CIELab` space using the `colorspacious` package. Given a sequence of colors, this tells you how different each pair of colors is. The placement of each color in the matrix is indicated by the color of the tick mark. The diagonal is white because this represents the color difference between a color with itself (which is zero or nan). Ideally, you want each color pair to have a high $\\Delta E*$, to ensure they are above the just-noticeable-difference (JND) threshold. When two colors are above the JND threshold, they are assumed to be differentiable in that colorblind space. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "c273bb8b-93ed-4efe-83c7-f4ead74c4ed0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1000x1000 with 8 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "_ = va.plot_color_deltaE('turbo6')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "05a38659-1ad8-42f6-8a94-3663b79894af",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We can also plot the normalized $\\Delta E*$ plots where we divide each cvd simulation $\\Delta E*$ matrix by the non cvd space matrix. While the above plot tells you how far two colors are in CIELab space, the normalized plot tells you how consistent differences between colors in a colorset are under colorblindness, as compared to how different they are when measured in the full colorspace. A $\\Delta E*$ of 1 means the pair's perceptual distance under CVD equals the distance under normal vision (no distinguishability loss). As we can see below, the visualastro `turbo6` colorset is colorblind safe!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "2cb856e1-f06b-4cc3-b542-4b404f68c8f8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1000x1000 with 8 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "_ = va.plot_color_deltaE('turbo6', normalize=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "469db792-2459-4565-84b6-7c36e9047036",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "If we look at ```rgb```, however, we can see that red and green suffer in both `'deuteranomaly'` and `'protanomaly'` colorspaces."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "c4b83828-1394-4cfb-ac5e-d154ebacd66b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1000x400 with 4 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(10,4))\n",
    "_ = va.plot_color_deltaE(['r', 'g', 'b'], cvd_type='deuteranomaly', ax=ax[0])\n",
    "_ = va.plot_color_deltaE(['r', 'g', 'b'], cvd_type='protanomaly', ax=ax[1])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2b74b96f-0f7e-447b-8c4a-660d4c4786f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
