    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3071e1de-30f1-4398-bdb2-31c4beba0639",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Color Collections"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b8093db0-7629-4e33-8e16-b63821c5ddb6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "There are many colors defined exclusively in VisualAstro. In addition to those, VisualAstro also recognizes all colors in Matplotlib, including \"base\" and \"tableau\" colors, and colors from the [xkcd color survey](https://xkcd.com/color/rgb/). The various recognized color collections, as well as all recognized colors, can be displayed using `va.help`:\n",
    "\n",
    "Individual color collections:\n",
    "* `va.help.va_colors()` → VisualAstro colors\n",
    "* `va.help.mpl_colors()` → Matplotlib named colors\n",
    "* `va.help.base_colors()` → Matplotlib base colors\n",
    "* `va.help.tableau_colors()` → Matplotlib tableau colors\n",
    "* `va.help.xkcd_colors()` → xkcd colors\n",
    "\n",
    "Large combined color collections, good for reference:\n",
    "* `va.help.named_colors()` → VisualAstro and Matplotlib named colors combined\n",
    "* `va.help.all_colors()` → all colors recognizable by VisualAstro\n",
    "\n",
    "Note that although xkcd colors are are only recognizable by Matplotlib with a \"xkcd:\" prefix, the prefix can be dropped in VisualAstro when there is no color in other color collections with the same name. In these `va.help` displays, the \"xkcd:\" prefix is dropped whenever possible. Read more about the xkcd color survey on the [xkcd blog](https://blog.xkcd.com/2010/05/03/color-survey-results/)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62dd9638-0203-4b31-b82a-052768ec95e0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### VisualAstro Colors"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "d0eca4ae-9a07-46b3-a711-3008e2e7a24a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
